                <pb facs="0527" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1100 Rogers, James H./38: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-05-18T11:00:00-04:00">May 18, 1934—11 a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>136. Reference your May 17, 5 p.m. Please inform Rogers urgently that discussion
                    with Chinese officials of possible loan involves traversing delicate political
                    ground. Department believes he should under no circumstances receive or discuss
                    any proposal for loan unless and until expressly instructed to do so. Department
                    expects to discuss portions of his telegram with Treasury today.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
